{
 "uid": "utm-obs-03-nodes",
 "title": "03 - Nodes & Cluster Resources",
 "description": "**Purpose:** Kubernetes node infrastructure health — CPU, memory, disk and node conditions.\n\n**Data sources:** Prometheus (node-exporter, kube-state-metrics).\n\n**Why disk leads this dashboard:** node root-filesystem exhaustion is this cluster's dominant failure mode. Ceph MONs raise MON_DISK_LOW below ~30% free, which degrades storage I/O, which causes Kubernetes liveness probes to time out, which produces cluster-wide restart storms.\n\n**Thresholds:** <70% healthy / 70-80% warning / 80-90% high / >90% critical. Adjust per panel field-config if your operational targets differ.\n\n**Drill-down:** high disk → *04 - Ceph & Storage*; high restarts → *01 - Platform Health*.",
 "tags": [
  "utm-observability",
  "nodes"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
 "editable": true,
